    "blisters": {
      "type": "content-columns",
      "settings": {
        "color_scheme": "paper",
        "layout": "stack",
        "numbered": false,
        "eyebrow": "Blisters",
        "heading": "What a dry foot does and does not prevent.",
        "lede": "<p>Waterproof socks help with blisters. They do not prevent them, and any brand telling you otherwise is selling you something.</p>",
        "mirror": false
      },
      "blocks": {
        "i1": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Wet skin blisters more easily",
            "body": "<p>Saturated skin softens and its resistance to friction drops sharply. Keeping the foot dry removes one of the three things a blister needs. That is a real and significant help.</p>"
          }
        },
        "i2": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Friction and fit still matter",
            "body": "<p>The other two things are pressure and movement. A boot that rubs will still rub. A sock that is too small will still bunch. No membrane changes that.</p>"
          }
        },
        "i3": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Grit is the one nobody mentions",
            "body": "<p>On wet ground, fine grit washes in over the cuff and sits under the foot. That is abrasive against skin and against the sock. Rinse both at the end of a wet day.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "i1",
        "i2",
        "i3"
      ]
    },
    "fit": {
      "type": "content-columns",
      "settings": {
        "color_scheme": "wash",
        "layout": "panel",
        "numbered": false,
        "eyebrow": "Fit",
        "heading": "Before you order, check the boot.",
        "lede": "<p>This is the question most sellers skip and most returns come from. Waterproof socks are thicker than the sock you are used to.</p>",
        "link_label": "The size bands in centimetres",
        "link_url": "/pages/size-guide",
        "mirror": false
      },
      "blocks": {
        "i1": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Roughly a mid-weight sock",
            "body": "<p>If your boots are already snug with a thick walking sock, they will be tight with these. If you wear a liner and a thick sock together, these replace both.</p>"
          }
        },
        "i2": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Take the larger band if you are between two",
            "body": "<p>A size down grips the toes, which is uncomfortable over eight hours and shortens the life of the membrane. Foot length, not shoe size, sets the band.</p>"
          }
        },
        "i3": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Lace pressure over the instep",
            "body": "<p>A thicker sock changes where a boot loads. Give the laces one honest adjustment on the first walk rather than assuming the fit is wrong.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "i1",
        "i2",
        "i3"
      ]
    },
